# Multi-agent lock board: several agents in one repo, each working inside files it has claimed, and checks that say when the working tree strays outside the claims.
# Subtasks are rows agents claim by writing their id into the owner
# column. Before touching files, an agent writes the globs it will edit
# into its claim cell (claim_agent_a = src/auth/**) and checks the other
# claims first; it clears its claim when done. Nothing enforces this; it
# works because every claim is visible, and the checks below watch what
# actually changed.
#
# `changed` is the working tree against the last commit, refreshed every
# few seconds. `unclaimed` lists changed files no claim covers (someone
# edited outside their area), `contested` lists files two claims cover
# (two agents may edit the same file), and `clear` is true when both are
# empty. Add a claim cell per agent, and add it to both checks' loops.
A1 = subtask
B1 = owner
C1 = status
A2 = refactor auth module
B2 =
C2 =
A3 = migrate db layer
B3 =
C3 =
claim_agent_a =
claim_agent_b =
changed = $ git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all -- . ':!.recalc' | cut -c4- # every: 3000
unclaimed = $ set -f; printf '%s\n' {changed} | while IFS= read -r f; do [ -z "$f" ] && continue; hit=0; for g in {claim_agent_a:raw} {claim_agent_b:raw}; do case "$f" in $g) hit=$((hit+1));; esac; done; [ $hit -eq 0 ] && echo "$f"; done; true
contested = $ set -f; printf '%s\n' {changed} | while IFS= read -r f; do [ -z "$f" ] && continue; hit=0; for g in {claim_agent_a:raw} {claim_agent_b:raw}; do case "$f" in $g) hit=$((hit+1));; esac; done; [ $hit -gt 1 ] && echo "$f"; done; true
clear = = and({unclaimed} == '', {contested} == '')
